/*--------------------------------*- Choupo -*--------------------------------*\
  chemistry/MgBOH4-formation.dat -- the magnesium borate ion pair, written from its masters:  Mg2+ + B(OH)3 + H2O = MgB(OH)4+ + H+

  logK25 = -7.84: the constant of the public-domain databank (pitzer.dat), which states no primary.  The paper
  (Felmy & Weare, Geochim. Cosmochim. Acta 50 (1986) 2771-2783) prints the standard chemical potential of the species, mu0/RT = -651.89 (Table 2, p. 2773);
  a constant needs the mu0 of the other species of the reaction as well, which are Harvie, Moller & Weare (1984)'s
  and are not in the literature folder, so the constant is NOT derived here: that waits for the primary.
  25 C only; the paper and the databank give no enthalpy, so none is written (a case at another temperature is
  announced by the engine as running outside the data).  The identity is the PITZER route's (D2): never mixed with
  the Davies route's  BOH4-formation  (logK -9.24 plus an enthalpy).
\*-----------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
recordType aqueousSpeciation;
schemaVersion 1;

species MgBOH4; masters ( { ion Mg; nu 1; } { ion H3BO3; nu 1; } { ion H; nu -1; } ); nuWater 1;
      logK25 -7.84; source "USGS PHREEQC pitzer.dat (public domain), log_k -7.84, delta_h 0 (not stated); the species' mu0/RT is -651.89 in Felmy & Weare, Geochim. Cosmochim. Acta 50 (1986) 2771-2783, Table 2, p. 2773";
